WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Speaker 1: We knew when the Supreme Court&nbsp;
overturned Roe v Wade that there would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.260
further actions when it comes to restricting&nbsp;
access to abortions at the state level. And one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:16.860
of the battle lines now is trying to essentially&nbsp;
banish abortion pills, as they're called,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:25.080
medication abortions from pharmacies in all&nbsp;
sorts of states around the country. And there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:32.760
now controversy involving involving Walgreens and&nbsp;
some other chains related to this. The relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.700
new governor of Massachusetts, Democrat Maura&nbsp;
Healey, has issued a declaration pharmacies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.480
must stock abortion pills. The Associated Press&nbsp;
reports the governor of Massachusetts reminded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:51.780
pharmacies Wednesday they are required to stock&nbsp;
a key abortion pill despite a nationwide effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.840
by anti-abortion activists to ban the medication.&nbsp;
The action comes as a federal judge in Texas is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.640
considering a lawsuit that would overturn&nbsp;
decades old federal approval of the drug.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.460
Democratic Governor Maura Healey issued a written&nbsp;
statement saying the pharmacies must maintain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.260
quote, a continuous sufficient supply&nbsp;
of all family planning medications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:20.280
including mifepristone, misoprostol, emergency&nbsp;
contraception and contraceptive prescriptions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:27.660
Now, this is great, but there's already very&nbsp;
little problem with abortion access in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.560
state of Massachusetts. But the most important&nbsp;
takeaway is that this is an action that trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.540
to block and ban and and prevent these drugs&nbsp;
from being available. This is being carried out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:48.180
by a political movement that claims to be pro-life&nbsp;
when this is actually an extraordinarily anti-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.920
thing to be doing. Limiting access to abortion&nbsp;
pills, which is the next sort of battle that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:59.100
they're fighting now. It's bad health policy&nbsp;
and it's also extraordinarily counterproductive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:06.900
to their own stated goals. Number one, abortion&nbsp;
pills are a safe and effective way to terminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:14.940
pregnancies in their early stages. When you limit&nbsp;
access to these drugs, it can lead to more unsafe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:21.300
methods of abortion, more dangerous methods&nbsp;
of abortion, and it can delay abortion until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:29.040
later in the pregnancy, which is never an ideal&nbsp;
thing to look for. It puts the health of women at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:36.120
risk. It can potentially put the lives of women&nbsp;
at risk. Unsafe abortions are a leading cause of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.520
maternal mortality worldwide. So when you limit&nbsp;
access to the abortion pills, you're essentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:47.220
forcing women either to have later abortions or&nbsp;
to have more dangerous abortions. And it's a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.760
bad thing when you look at the health data. Now,&nbsp;
of course, the people that are against the pills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.620
don't care. And to some degree, they believe if we&nbsp;
limit access to these pills, a lot of these women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:02.160
simply won't have abortions altogether. But we can&nbsp;
talk about that as well when you limit access to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:09.900
abortion pills. There's the philosophical issue,&nbsp;
which is you're violating the bodily autonomy of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:16.140
these women. Women should have the right to have&nbsp;
these tools available and to decide with freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.940
and liberty. Is this something I want to use&nbsp;
or not? Let me make a decision about my body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:28.500
and my health with the doctors. When you limit&nbsp;
access to these medications, you violate that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.540
fundamental principle of freedom, liberty and&nbsp;
bodily autonomy, which these right wingers claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:41.940
to defend. But then let's go to the end. Okay.&nbsp;
Think of the economic and social consequences of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:48.420
this. If you succeed, if you succeed at preventing&nbsp;
abortions by making the pills difficult to access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:55.380
Women. If they choose not to have the if&nbsp;
they're unable to have the abortion because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:01.680
you limit access to these pills, they might&nbsp;
end up carrying to term and ending up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:07.440
a child that they were unprepared for or&nbsp;
for whatever reason did not want to have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:14.220
You then have a situation where and I know that&nbsp;
this sounds so cold, right? But the economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:21.840
impact, you are now going to have individuals&nbsp;
who will lose income due to time off, suffer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:27.360
economic hardships, people who have children that&nbsp;
they don't want to have. The outcomes aren't good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.800
for the parents and they're not not good for&nbsp;
the kids. And so then you lose the economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:37.320
productivity of that person. It sounds crazy&nbsp;
to even be talking about it, but this is part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:42.900
of their entire thing. If if that's something&nbsp;
you care about, then your actions in trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:48.780
ban these pills are counterproductive. Not to&nbsp;
mention for those pregnant mothers who do have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:54.240
the ability to go to another state, for example,&nbsp;
to obtain the pills or obtain a surgical abortion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.400
Now they are going to have to take time off. And&nbsp;
that's going to have an economic impact as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.600
So no matter what you care about, whether you care&nbsp;
about philosophy and ethics, liberty and freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.800
whether you care about safety, whether you care&nbsp;
about economic product, whatever you care about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.500
Trying to prevent access to these&nbsp;
medications makes no sense whatsoever

